{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>And they shall be on Aharon and on his sons.</b> The sense of the verse is: they shall be on Aharon — the eight priestly garments mentioned from the beginning of the parashah until here, which are the חושן and the אפוד and the מעיל and the כתונת תשבץ, the מצנפת and the אבנט and the ציץ and the מכנסי בד; and on his sons — the four garments of the ordinary priest. And this is what is written: 'ולא ישאו עון ומתו' — for a High Priest who served with fewer than eight, or an ordinary priest who served with fewer than four, is called deficient in garments, and if he performed his service it is invalid and he is liable to death at the hand of Heaven, like a stranger who served, as it is said: ״וחגרת אותם אבנט אהרן ובניו וגו׳ והיתה להם כהונה לחקת עולם״ — when their garments are upon them, their priesthood is upon them; when their garments are not upon them, their priesthood is not upon them, and they are like strangers. And it is written: ״והזר הקרב יומת״." "<b>An everlasting statute for him and for his seed after him.</b> That the High Priest wears eight garments during the service and the ordinary priest four during the service, and they are: מכנסי בד, כתנת, מצנפת, and אבנט. And there was a great wonder among the priests who offered sacrifices every day: their body was clothed only in the כתנת alone, which is a tunic, and they endured the cold in the rainy season and did not die. Therefore our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said that they would appoint over the priests an official to inspect them and treat their ailments, for most of them were ill from intestinal illness, because their service all the days of the year was in the tunic alone during the service, and furthermore they stood constantly on the floor and were barefoot."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ולא ישאו עון ומתו' ('and they shall not bear iniquity and die') appears here as a quotation; however, the actual phrase at the end of Exodus 28:43 reads 'ולא ישאו עון ומתו' only in some witnesses — R. Bahya may be quoting it from memory or paraphrasing the verse's conclusion."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:24.228771593Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}